        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(qa): move restart and policy scenarios to YAML",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a QA ownership problem where restart/resume, replay dedupe, allowlist reload, WhatsApp access-policy, and pairing-gate coverage remained split across imperative channel runtimes instead of the canonical scenario catalog and shared flow host.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMoves the assigned behavior family into canonical YAML flow scenarios for Slack, WhatsApp, and Matrix, while keeping transport-native evidence only where normalized state is insufficient. The change deletes the replaced imperative owners and obsolete tests, adds the minimal Matrix observer and WhatsApp group adapter support needed by shared flows, and teaches the shared config-mutation host how to observe intentionally deferred restarts.\n\nTelegram was inventoried and has no imperative owner in this behavior family. Routing, commands, threads, and infrastructure lanes are unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nQA maintainers can run these restart and configuration behaviors through one canonical catalog and shared execution path across QA Channel, live adapters, and Crabline. This reduces duplicate scenario logic and makes parity gaps visible in YAML rather than channel-specific runtime code.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kww4yt1d8bdx7f9n025as70g` (`quick-crab`), provider `blacksmith-testbox`.\n- Focused validation: 265 tests passed across QA Lab and Matrix scenario/runtime suites.\n- QA Channel: `slack-restart-resume` passed with mock OpenAI.\n- Crabline bridge: `matrix-restart-resume` passed.\n- Canonical live Matrix adapter: restart/resume, post-restart continuation, replay dedupe, and allowlist hot reload passed 4/4.\n- Review-fix reruns: replay dedupe and allowlist hot reload each passed independently after parity corrections.\n- Formatting: `oxfmt --check` passed for all 26 changed files.\n- Autoreview: `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --stream-engine-output` returned clean with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Exact-head delegated `check:changed` reached full typecheck; the remote sparse-sync checkout omitted tracked `extensions/qa-lab/src/mantis/**`, producing only `Cannot find module './mantis/cli.js'`. Hosted CI uses a full checkout and remains the authoritative exact-head broad gate.\n",
        "branch": "dallin/wave2-channel-restart-config",
